                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Its a straight up clone of Kingdom. \n\nIt does have some improvements over Kingdom like knowing how much money is in your bank and how much interest you're earning, but not just the concept or gameplay was copied. The cost of walls and units, the cost of hiring new villagers, even the jobs you train your people to do, with the single exception of the worthless woodcutter, at least in Kingdom your builders chop your trees.\n\nLet me quote the devs for you:\n\nMcMagic Productions  [developer] Mar 16, 2019 @ 12:17pm \nOriginally posted by Xariot:\n\"As long as you add new things and make the game your own there's really not a problem with making a game inspired by another game, just be cautious of 1:1 feature copy. Just making it in a 3D engine with everything else playing exactly the same isn't enough to say it's a different game.\n\nLook at Satisfactory compared to Factorio. The games are clearly similar but the aren't identical in features. Enough is different between the two of them beyond just 2D and 3D for them to happily exist without one being seen as a total copy of the other.\n\nAdd new things you wished were in Kingdom, fix issues that made the gameplay less enjoyable. Make it your own and it will be a good game, not just a 3D looking copy.\n\nI don't think most people will care the concept might seem \"copied\" from Kingdom if you change enough to make it your own. But starting off making a 1:1 copy of a game is a good start, just take it to that next level and you'll have a great spiritual successor to Kingdom.\" \n\nDev's response:\n\"That's exactly what our plan is.\nThe basic concept is the same, but other things are and will be according to our ideas.\"\n\nBasic concept is the same? No, all concepts are the same. I can count the differences on one hand. You took what someone else did, copied it exactly, changed a few minor things (yes improvements, I agree) and you are now making money off of someone else's work. I'm all for expanding the genre but this is plagiarism. \n\nGranted there's more content in Kingdom than in this, which is why it's getting a negative review. This should be an early access game -- not a fully released game, McMagic Productions should be ashamed, or better yet, shut down.\n\nIt's also so similar to Kingdom that Noio, Licorice should seriously consider contacting a lawyer or request that steam removes the 95% clone.",
